1
00:00:15,789 --> 00:00:21,789
A snowman longs to break out of his snow globe.

2
00:00:31,578 --> 00:00:37,578
Knick Knack is a animation, family, comedy film directed by John Lasseter.

3
00:00:47,368 --> 00:00:53,368
Life on a shelf as a snowman trapped in a snow-globe blizzard can become wearing,
especially when you're surrounded by knickknacks from sunnier locales.

4
00:01:03,157 --> 00:01:09,157
When the jaded snowman finally breaks free of his glass
house, his vacation plans are cut short.

5
00:01:18,947 --> 00:01:24,947
Knick Knack is a 1989 American animated short film produced by
Pixar that was written and directed by John Lasseter.

6
00:01:34,736 --> 00:01:40,736
The short is about a snow globe snowman who wants to join the
other travel souvenirs in a summer-themed party.

7
00:01:50,526 --> 00:01:56,526
However, the glass dome that surrounds him prevents him from doing so, thus
leading to his many tries to break out of his snow globe.

8
00:02:06,315 --> 00:02:12,315
Knick Knack is Pixar's fourth short and the final short produced
during the company's tenure as a hardware company.

9
00:02:22,105 --> 00:02:28,105
It was also the final Pixar short film released before the
company's first feature-length film Toy Story.

10
00:02:37,894 --> 00:02:43,894
The short stands out from Lasseter's other early short films at Pixar
in its reliance on pure comedy to drive the story.

11
00:02:53,684 --> 00:02:59,684
It was inspired by Tom and Jerry, Looney Tunes, and the
work of animators Chuck Jones and Tex Avery.

12
00:03:09,473 --> 00:03:15,473
Lasseter and his wife, Nancy, collected snow globes and also enjoyed souvenirs from
distant places and those elements made their way into the short as well.

13
00:03:25,263 --> 00:03:31,263
Singer Bobby McFerrin improvised the a cappella vocal jazz soundtrack to the film while
watching a rough cut which was eventually left unchanged in its final edition.

14
00:03:41,052 --> 00:03:47,052
Knick Knack debuted at the 1989 SIGGRAPH convention in
Boston, Massachusetts and was presented in 3D.

15
00:03:56,842 --> 00:04:02,842
The short has enjoyed positive reviews since its debut and has
been screened as a part of numerous film festivals.

16
00:04:12,631 --> 00:04:18,631
The short has now been associated with Finding Nemo, with a remastered version of the
short being shown before it in that film's original theatrical run.

17
00:04:28,421 --> 00:04:34,421
The film explores themes of escape, snowman, snowglobes, short film.

18
00:04:44,210 --> 00:04:50,210
The tone is lighthearted.
